Confirmed as stated, with one fix to the evidence: "epsilon" appears on V1 lines 263 and 286, not only 286. Line 263 ("no historical epsilon") means a historical tolerance and defines nothing, so epsilon in "a>2epsilon" (line 286) is still undefined. It is WORD_POLYNOMIAL's epsilon=eta+B (= the protocol's e_i), and the guard should read a_j>d_i=2e_i (P15), alongside a_j>2delta (P8).

The symbol clashes listed are all real:
- g_j: the distance in P19 (line 204/206) versus the bracket half-width in the ledger (lines 236/239);
- T_j (line 239) versus T_Q,I (P11);
- Q: the clip cap versus the grid diagram Q_i (line 118, P15) versus a random variable (line 78);
- rho: a density (lines 35, 88) versus the coupling bound (line 100, P7);
- H: the height unit versus H(t) versus H_I.

Each formula is correct when read with its nearest definition, so the fix is editorial: rename P19's distance and the Section 9 theory sum, separate the cap from the diagram symbol, and translate epsilon into protocol symbols.
